# Auto commit and push

After completing any code update in this project:

1. Commit all relevant changes with a concise message (focus on why, not what).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch without waiting for the user to ask.
3. **Always update the server.** Push to `main` auto-deploys on Coolify (app `MAHALLA90`, uuid `kkkfxb8t2hlzk1f9t4d2wjct`). After the push, wait for the deployment to finish and verify it:
   - `~/.local/bin/coolify app deployments list kkkfxb8t2hlzk1f9t4d2wjct --format json` → newest row must be `finished` with the pushed commit;
   - if no deployment was triggered, start it: `~/.local/bin/coolify deploy uuid kkkfxb8t2hlzk1f9t4d2wjct`;
   - `curl -s https://tandoor.budavron.uz/api/health` → `"ready":true`.
4. In the final reply give the commit hash, state that the deploy finished, and **always include the production link `https://tandoor.budavron.uz`** (plus the specific page, e.g. `https://tandoor.budavron.uz/prihod`).

Do not commit files with secrets (`.env`, credentials). Do not force-push to main.

If there are no changes to commit, skip commit/push and say so.
